-- title:
--   Chart image equals swap-invariant subring of the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and let $R_\pi := \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W / (X_0X_1 - C(\pi))$ be the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $W$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi)$. Assume: $W$ is precomplete for the $\pi$-adic filtration, i.e. for the ideal `Ideal.span {π}`; the element $X_0X_1 - C(\pi)$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ (hypothesis `hreg`); and $R_\pi$ is separated for the ideal generated by `const π π`, the class of $C(\pi)$, in the sense that any $x \in R_\pi$ lying in $(\,\mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi\,)^B$ for every $B \in \mathbb{N}$ is zero (hypothesis `hsep`). Let `chartHom π : PowerSeries W →+* UVCrossingModel W π` be the ring homomorphism substituting the distinguished two-variable series `sAmbient` for the variable of a one-variable power series and then passing to the quotient. Then the image subring of `chartHom π` coincides with `fixedSubring π`, the equaliser of the involution `crossingSwap π` (induced on the quotient by interchanging the two variables, which preserves the ideal) with the identity, i.e. with the subring of elements fixed by that involution.
--
--   This identifies the invariants of the branch-exchange involution on the standard crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, the completed local ring at a crossing point of a modular curve, with the image of the one-parameter chart; classically it is the statement that the fixed locus of the involution exchanging the two branches is described by the symmetric coordinate. It feeds the structural results on the crossing model, including the presentations of the fixed subring as a quotient of a polynomial ring by a monic polynomial and the accompanying length and rank computations.
